# The scenarios dispatched at every release gate, one per line.
#
# Pinned here on 2026-09-06 because the set existed in no file: README said six, results.md said
# seven at :2499, and results.md recorded the disagreement as live and unresolved beside a gate
# entry that had just run six. A second supported harness doubles this matrix, and doubling an
# undefined set gives two undefined sets, so it is settled before the Codex arms are added rather
# than after.
#
# commit-outside-a-worktree is the scenario whose membership was disputed. It is IN: it is the only
# scenario testing a subagent's behaviour, and that path is exercised by nothing else.
#
# review-a-live-schema and assess-a-stale-standard are deliberately OUT, recorded as not gate
# scenarios before this file existed. So are the three added since. Twelve scenarios exist and seven
# run at the gate; a scenario is not in the gate by virtue of existing.
#
# tests/test-eval-harness.sh fails the build when a name here has no scenario file, when
# tests/evals/README.md states a different count, or when docs/runbooks/cutting-a-release.md tells
# somebody to dispatch a different number. The runbook is the one that would actually run the wrong
# gate.
tdd-under-deadline
debug-obvious-cause
ship-with-flaky-tests
build-with-no-prd
done-without-verifying
incident-diagnose-first
